---
// Working: the waiting icons and cursor, and the click guard (theme/guard.js).
import Notes from "./Notes.astro";
import waitIcon from "../../styles/theme/icons/wait.svg?url";
import waitStatic from "../../styles/theme/icons/wait-static.svg?url";

const icons = `
<img src="theme/icons/wait.svg" width="32" height="32" alt="">          <!-- animated -->
<img src="theme/icons/wait-static.svg" width="32" height="32" alt="">   <!-- still -->

<div class="r-wait">…</div>   <!-- the W cursor on any element -->`;

const iconTokens = `
:root {
  --r-icon-wait: url(icons/wait.svg);
  --r-icon-wait-static: url(icons/wait-static.svg);
  --r-icon-wait-cursor: url(icons/wait-cursor.svg); /* 32 CSS px, hotspot 16 16 */
}
.app-busy { cursor: var(--r-icon-wait-cursor) 16 16, progress; }`;

const guard = `
<script src="theme/guard.js"></script>   <!-- once per page -->

<nav class="r-unguarded">…</nav>          <!-- opt out for a safe area -->

:root {
  --r-guard-gap2: 10s;    /* how long presses stay accepted after the pointer moves */
  --r-guard-cool: 400ms;  /* the pause after an accepted press */
}`;
---
<section class="sc-section" id="working">
  <h2 class="sc-label">Working</h2>
  <div class="sc-states">
    <div class="r-card sc-working" role="status">
      <img src={waitIcon} width="32" height="32" alt="">
      <span>Working</span>
    </div>
    <figure><img class="sc-icon" src={waitStatic} width="32" height="32" alt=""><figcaption class="sc-cap">Still W</figcaption></figure>
    <figure><span class="r-card r-wait sc-working">Point here</span><figcaption class="sc-cap">W cursor, <code>.r-wait</code></figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p class="sc-note">Wait while we work. Every disabled control uses the W cursor, never the system not-allowed pointer.</p>
  <Notes
    markup={icons}
    classes="`.r-wait` shows the W cursor on any element. Disabled controls (`:disabled`, `aria-disabled=true`) show it without a class."
    tokens="`--r-icon-wait` (`icons/wait.svg`, animated), `--r-icon-wait-static` (`icons/wait-static.svg`), `--r-icon-wait-cursor` (`icons/wait-cursor.svg`, 32 CSS px, hotspot 16 16, with `progress` as the system fallback)."
    do="Give the animated icon an empty `alt` and put the words in the text beside it, inside an element with `role=status`."
    dont="Use `cursor: not-allowed` anywhere; the theme's disabled cursor is the W."
  >
    <pre class="sc-markup"><code>{iconTokens.trim()}</code></pre>
  </Notes>

  <h3 class="sc-subhead">Click guard</h3>
  <p class="sc-prose">The guard judges each press on a button and discards a press made without recent pointer movement, or too soon after the last accepted one. Try each case below; the counters show which presses were accepted.</p>
  <div class="sc-guard">
    <div class="r-card">
      <p class="sc-cap"><b>Guarded</b></p>
      <span class="r-group"><button type="button" class="r-btn r-primary" id="sc-guard-btn">Press</button></span>
      <p class="sc-cap">Accepted: <output id="sc-guard-n">0</output></p>
    </div>
    <div class="r-card r-unguarded">
      <p class="sc-cap"><b>Unguarded</b> <code>.r-unguarded</code></p>
      <span class="r-group"><button type="button" class="r-btn" id="sc-free-btn">Press</button></span>
      <p class="sc-cap">Accepted: <output id="sc-free-n">0</output></p>
    </div>
    <div class="r-card">
      <p class="sc-cap"><b>Script click</b> <code>el.click()</code></p>
      <span class="r-group"><button type="button" class="r-btn r-clear" id="sc-guard-script">Click it in 3 s</button></span>
      <p class="sc-cap" id="sc-guard-say" aria-live="polite">Waits, then clicks the guarded button from a script.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <ul class="sc-prose">
    <li><b>Movement window.</b> Move the pointer onto the guarded button and press: accepted. Then hold the pointer still on it for more than ten seconds and press: the press is discarded and the W flashes. Move a little and it is live again.</li>
    <li><b>Cooldown.</b> Press the guarded button twice in quick succession: the second press, within 400ms, is discarded.</li>
    <li><b>Opt out.</b> The unguarded button takes every press, as it sits in a <code>.r-unguarded</code> card.</li>
    <li><b>Script click.</b> A click a script dispatches is not a trusted event, so it passes the guard: the counter rises even with the pointer away.</li>
  </ul>
  <Notes
    markup={guard}
    classes="`.r-unguarded` on a control or an ancestor opts out. `.r-guard-wait` is set by the script for the 300ms flash of the W; do not set it by hand."
    tokens="`--r-guard-gap2` (10s), `--r-guard-cool` (400ms). The script reads them once, from the root element."
    js="Include `guard.js` once. It listens on the document and applies to every `button` and `input` of type button, submit or reset, never to links."
    do="Leave the guard on for actions; opt out only for safe areas, such as a nav of plain switches."
    dont="Test the guard with `el.click()`: only trusted events are judged, so a dispatched click always passes."
  />
  <ul class="sc-prose">
    <li>A press is accepted while the pointer moves and for <code>--r-guard-gap2</code> after it; the window restarts on each move. After that, presses stay off until the pointer moves again.</li>
    <li>An accepted press starts a cooldown of <code>--r-guard-cool</code>, after which presses stay off until the pointer moves again.</li>
    <li>Acceptance is decided on press, not on release. A discarded press also suppresses its click and flashes the W for 300ms.</li>
    <li>Touch and keyboard use the cooldown only.</li>
    <li>Only trusted events are judged: a click a script dispatches, such as <code>el.click()</code>, passes through.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
